!
! Hours to a machine part's next service (ratchet_rules.h RR4), in
! Trebago, one part per row: a service is due every `interval` full-load
! hours (1 .. 999999), the part has worn `worn` load-hours since the last
! (RR3, 0 .. 999999999999999) and runs at `load` (1 .. 10000 hundredths of
! a percent), so at that load it has (interval * 10000 - worn) / load
! hours left, an exact fraction; below 0 the service is past due. ok is
! 0 outside the domain, and the division by it refuses the row.
trebago service
  in  interval(n), worn(n), load(n)
  out left(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, interval(i))) * min(1, max(0, 999999 - interval(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, worn(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 999999999999999 - worn(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, load(i))) * min(1, max(0, 10000 - load(i) + 1))
  left(i) = (interval(i) * 10000 - worn(i)) / (load(i) * ok(i))
end
